n"}},{"type":"text","value":" and your lockfile, recognises the framework, bundler and\npackage manager, and shows every change it would make as a diff: the configuration\nfile, the adapter in your bundler's configuration, the stylesheet and the "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":"\ntypes. Nothing is written until you say yes, and the install command is\nprinted for you to run (or pass "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--install</span>","source":"--install"}},{"type":"text","value":"). Then:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style doctor","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style doctor","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"checks the engine, the installed versions, the configuration and the wiring, and\nsays what is missing. Both are described in "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/cli#kirana-style-init","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the CLI"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"init","source":"init"}},{"type":"text","value":" adds "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span>","source":"kirana-style"}},{"type":"text","value":" to your dev dependencies, so every later command runs\nthe version your project pins: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style check","source":"npx kirana-style check"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style build","source":"npx kirana-style build"}},{"type":"text","value":"\nand the rest. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/cli#a-shorter-name","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A shorter name"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is one script away."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pick-your-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick your framework"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each guide takes you from an empty project to a styled component, and names the\nexample that CI builds and checks in a browser on every change."}]},{"type":"component","name":"frameworks","attributes":{},"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The overview of all of them, with what "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" compiles to in each, is\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/frameworks/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"supported frameworks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install-by-hand","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install by hand"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The runtime package, the command line and your bundler's adapter (Vite here; your\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#pick-your-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" names yours):"}]},{"type":"component","name":"install","attributes":{"packages":"@kirana-style/core","dev":"kirana-style @kirana-style/vite"},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"machines-without-a-native-build","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Machines without a native build"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine is native code for eight platforms. Anywhere else (a WebContainer, an\nunusual CPU), install its WebAssembly build as well; Kirana uses it when no native\nengine loads, and it writes exactly the same CSS, about twice as slowly:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npm install -D @kirana-style/compiler-wasm32-wasi --force","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npm</span> install <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">-D</span> @kirana-style/compiler-wasm32-wasi <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--force</span>","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-type\">KIRANA_FORCE_WASI</span>=<span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span>","source":"KIRANA_FORCE_WASI=1"}},{"type":"text","value":" uses it even where the native engine works."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-every-setup-has","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What every setup has"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The guides differ in names, not in shape. Whatever the framework, a project needs\nthe same four things."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-the-bundler-plugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. The bundler plugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana compiles modules, so it runs in the bundler, ahead of the framework's own\nplugin. Here it is for React on Vite 8; the "},{"type":"link","href":"#pick-your-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"guides"}]},{"type":"text","value":" show it\nfor every other framework and bundler."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import { defineConfig } from \"vite\"\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\"\nimport kirana from \"@kirana-style/vite\"\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  // Kirana goes before the framework plugins, so they only ever see compiled\n  // JavaScript.\n  plugins: [kirana(), react()],\n})","lang":"ts","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { defineConfig } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;vite&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> react <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@vitejs/plugin-react&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> kirana <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/vite&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineConfig</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// Kirana goes before the framework plugins, so they only ever see compiled</span>\n  <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// JavaScript.</span>\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">plugins</span>: [<span class=\"th-token th-function\">kirana</span>(), <span class=\"th-token th-function\">react</span>()],\n})","file":"vite.config.ts","title":"vite.config.ts"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-the-configuration-file","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. The configuration file"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"kirana.config.ts","source":"kirana.config.ts"}},{"type":"text","value":" sits in the project root. It is optional, since every key has a\ndefault, but this is where layers, targets and diagnostic levels live."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import { defineConfig } from \"@kirana-style/core/config\"\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  // Your own layers, placed below every Kirana rule.\n  layers: { before: [\"reset\", \"base\"] },\n})","lang":"ts","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { defineConfig } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/core/config&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineConfig</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// Your own layers, placed below every Kirana rule.</span>\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">layers</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">before</span>: [<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;reset&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;base&quot;</span>] },\n})","file":"kirana.config.ts","title":"kirana.config.ts"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every key is listed in the "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/config/reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"configuration reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-the-stylesheet-entry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. The stylesheet entry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana writes one stylesheet. Import it once, in your entry, before your own\nglobal CSS, and the adapter fills it in:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import \"@kirana-style/core/stylesheet.css\"","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/core/stylesheet.css&quot;</span>","file":"src/main.tsx","title":"src/main.tsx"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A framework that renders the whole document as a component, such as\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/frameworks/tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":", links it from that component\ninstead:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import kiranaCss from \"@kirana-style/core/stylesheet.css?url\"\n\n// Before your own global stylesheet: its `@layer reset, base, kirana`\n// statement fixes the layer order.\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href={kiranaCss} />","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> kiranaCss <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/core/stylesheet.css?url&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// Before your own global stylesheet: its `@layer reset, base, kirana`</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// statement fixes the layer order.</span>\n&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">link</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">rel</span>=<span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;stylesheet&quot;</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">href</span>={kiranaCss} /&gt;","file":"root.tsx","title":"root.tsx"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your framework's guide shows which of the two it uses."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In development the adapter serves the live stylesheet and updates it over HMR. In\na production build it replaces the placeholder rule and renames the file to a\ncontent hash."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-the-sx-prop-s-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sx"},{"type":"text","value":" prop's types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" is not an 